<Layouts.public flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <.header>
      Terms of Service
      <:subtitle>The agreement between you and FluxVale.</:subtitle>
    </.header>

    <p class="text-xs text-ink-subtle">
      Last updated: <!-- set at merge -->
    </p>

    <%!-- #365: the terms' text of record. Plain English, not gettext —
        this template is the contract's wording. The decided parameters
        (entity, Philippines law and venue, admin@fluxvale.com, the
        12-month liability cap, the non-committal data-deletion line)
        are the maintainer's, Nov 3 2026 — they are decisions, not
        placeholders. Advisory edits land here. --%>
    <.card class="space-y-4" data-testid="terms-of-service">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">About these terms</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        These terms are an agreement between you and FLUXVALE INFORMATION
        SOLUTIONS OPC, a Philippine One Person Corporation ("FluxVale",
        "we", "us").
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        You accept them when you create an account or top up your wallet.
        If you use FluxVale on behalf of someone else, you accept them
        for that person too.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We may change these terms. We give notice before a change applies
        — by email or a note in the app. Changes required by law, or
        needed to keep the service safe, can apply sooner.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">The service</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        FluxVale is a managed cloud platform for open source apps. You
        pick an app from our curated catalog, deploy it in one guided
        flow, and we run it for you: platform-managed runtimes, updates,
        monitoring, TLS, and backups. Each instance runs at the resource
        size you choose. There is no root or server access — managing
        the servers is our job.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Networking: a public instance serves at a fluxvale.app subdomain.
        A private instance has no public address at all — it is reachable
        only through your own private network, from your own devices.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Your account</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Give accurate information and keep your credentials safe. You are
        responsible for what happens through your account. You must be
        able to form a binding contract where you live.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Credits and payment</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        FluxVale runs on a prepaid wallet. You top up, we deduct credits
        as your instances run, and credits never expire. Credits are
        non-refundable —
        <.link
          navigate={~p"/policies/refund"}
          class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink"
        >
          the refund policy
        </.link>
        is the full stance and is part of these terms.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We don't store card details on the platform — payments run
        through a payment provider.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        An exhausted balance suspends your instances instead of accruing debt.
        Nothing is ever charged recurrently; a top-up happens only
        when you complete one yourself.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        You must follow the <.link
          navigate={~p"/policies/acceptable-use"}
          class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink"
        >
          Acceptable Use Policy
        </.link>. It is part of these terms. We can suspend or terminate
        accounts that break it.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Your apps and data</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Your content stays yours. You are responsible for what you deploy
        and for what you do with it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        The apps in the catalog are open-source projects under their own
        licenses. Meeting those licenses for your use is your
        responsibility.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We can suspend or terminate your account or an instance for
        breaking the Acceptable Use Policy, for an exhausted balance, or
        for a long-abandoned account. You can stop using FluxVale at any
        time and take your data with you.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        When an account or instance ends, it stops serving.
        We may delete your data after termination.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Changes to the service</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        The catalog and the service change over time: apps join, apps
        leave, features improve. We give notice where practical, and we
        warn you before retiring an app you run.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Intellectual property</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        The platform — the site, the catalog, the tooling — belongs to
        FluxVale. Your apps and your data belong to you. The open-source
        apps keep their own licenses and belong to their projects.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Disclaimers</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        The service is provided as-is. We work hard to keep it running,
        but we don't promise uninterrupted or error-free service.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        To the extent the law allows, FluxVale is not liable for indirect
        or consequential damages. Our total liability for a claim is
        capped at the amounts you paid us in the
        12 months before that claim.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Indemnity</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        If your use of FluxVale breaks the law, the Acceptable Use
        Policy, or someone else's rights, you cover the resulting claims
        against us.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        These terms follow the laws of the Philippines. Disputes go to
        the courts of the Philippines.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">General</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We send notices to the email on your account. These terms, the
        Acceptable Use Policy, and the refund policy are the whole
        agreement between you and us.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        You can't assign this agreement without our OK; we can assign it
        as part of the business. If a term turns out unenforceable, the
        rest still applies.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Questions about these terms: admin@fluxvale.com
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</Layouts.public>
